{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And if one soul sins inadvertently.</b> Idolatry was included among all the commandments for which an individual brings a ewe or a she-goat, a leader a he-goat, and an anointed priest and a court a bull. Scripture now removes it from all of them to be stringent concerning it and to rule by a fixed standard that an individual, a leader, and an anointed one bring for it <b>a she-goat in its first year for a sin-offering</b>. Therefore this section was stated." "<b>A she-goat in its first year.</b> This is a general principle: wherever 'she-goat' is stated, it must be in its first year."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The acronyms ב״‎ד and משוח resolved as 'court' (בית דין) and 'anointed one' (משוח) respectively, following the standard sacrificial categories."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:06.499842914Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}